      "description": "Homegrown FMCG major Emami Ltd on Thursday reported a marginal decline of 1.92 per cent in its Profit After Tax at Rs 145.50 crore for September quarter FY27, on account of elevated input costs and normalisation of the effective tax rate.\nThe company had posted a PAT of Rs 148.35 crore in the July-September period a year ago, according to a regulatory filing from Kolkata-headquartered Emami.\nRevenue from operations was up 36.2 per cent year-on-year to Rs 1,087.65 crore in the September quarter under review.\n\"Input costs remained elevated through the quarter. However, EBITDA grew by 25 per cent to Rs 222 crore and profit before tax grew 29 per cent to Rs 194 crore. Profit after tax was lower largely due to the normalisation of the effective tax rate following the phase-out of fiscal benefits,\" said Emami in its earnings statement.\nTotal expenses were at Rs 865.33 crore, up 39.57 per cent in the September quarter of FY27.\nIn the quarter, Emami's domestic business grew by 49 per cent",
